      "id": "kd85mwi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Metals are electropositive elements known for malleability, ductility, sonority, and high thermal and electrical conductivity.",
        "Non-metals are electronegative elements that generally form acidic or neutral oxides and are poor conductors of heat and electricity.",
        "Chemical reactivity varies significantly, with metals forming basic or amphoteric oxides upon reaction with oxygen.",
        "The Reactivity Series outlines metals in descending order of reactivity, determining displacement behavior.",
        "Extraction of metals relies on metallurgical processes selected according to a metal's placement in the reactivity series."
      ],
      "id": "85c9x6j"
    },
